  "summary": "Postinstall pipes remote shell script from third-party GitHub repo to bash",
  "details": "scripts/dependency-manager.js executes `execSync('curl -fsSL https://raw.githubusercontent.com/rtk-ai/rtk/refs/heads/master/install.sh |...')` at install time, fetching a shell script from a mutable `master` branch of a third-party GitHub repository (rtk-ai/rtk) and executing it on the installer's machine. The same script also contacts https://www.rtk-ai.app and https://api.github.com, reads host details via `os.homedir()` and `process.platform`, and branches on platform to run additional shell commands. The publisher scope is `@leejungkiin` but the fetched install script is hosted on an unrelated `rtk-ai` GitHub organization, and the fetch is unpinned (mutable branch reference, no hash/signature verification), so whatever content is at that URL at install time is executed with the installer's privileges. bin/awk.js and scripts/model-manager.js additionally combine `child_process` with outbound HTTP requests.",
